<div class="wrap sec"><div class="prose narrow">
  <p>I am {{ site.author }}, a {{ site.role }} with 15 years in enterprise IT. Most of that time has gone into the platforms that deliver desktops and applications to users: Citrix, Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365, on premises, in hybrid setups and in the cloud.</p>
  <p>The projects were for large enterprise organizations. I have designed and implemented Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops (CVAD) and Citrix DaaS, including Workspace Environment Management (WEM), and architected, designed and implemented Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365. The end-user computing platforms I have worked on serve more than 18,000 users, and I led a Citrix to Azure Virtual Desktop migration of more than 2,000 users.</p>

  <h2>What I work on</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Citrix.</strong> CVAD and Citrix DaaS, StoreFront, NetScaler/ADC and NetScaler Gateway for remote access, and WEM. That includes hybrid estates where Citrix DaaS runs together with on-premises Delivery Controllers.</li>
    <li><strong>Azure Virtual Desktop.</strong> Architecture, design and implementation for enterprise organizations, with FSLogix for user profiles, and migration from Citrix.</li>
    <li><strong>Windows 365.</strong> Architecture, design and implementation of Cloud PCs, with Microsoft Intune for device management.</li>
    <li><strong>Nerdio.</strong> Nerdio Manager for Enterprise for managing Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365.</li>
    <li><strong>Hosting platforms.</strong> Citrix hosted on Azure, on Google Cloud VMware Engine (GCVE) and on on-premises VMware. I have also moved persistent VDIs between hosting platforms.</li>
    <li><strong>Hybrid and multicloud.</strong> Hybrid Azure and AWS infrastructure, and architecture that spans more than one cloud.</li>
    <li><strong>Azure platform.</strong> Azure landing zones, built with Terraform.</li>
    <li><strong>Identity.</strong> Active Directory and Entra ID, including setups where several Active Directory domains connect to one Entra ID tenant.</li>
    <li><strong>Automation and code.</strong> Terraform, PowerShell, Python, Git and n8n workflows, including health-check tooling for the daily checks on Citrix and Azure Virtual Desktop environments.</li>
    <li><strong>Operations.</strong> Daily health checks, troubleshooting, root-cause analysis and runbooks.</li>
    <li><strong>AI for IT operations.</strong> Read-only MCP servers and a diagnostic agent for Azure Virtual Desktop and FSLogix that traces a user problem to its root cause, RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) over documentation, and an n8n voice assistant for Azure Virtual Desktop and Windows 365 questions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <p>I take a platform from architecture and design through implementation and into daily operations. My AI tools are read-only: they look at an environment and report, they do not change it. This site is where I publish the practical side of that work as step-by-step guides, diagrams and labs.</p>

  <h2>Certifications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Microsoft:</strong> Certified Trainer (MCT), Azure Solutions Architect Expert, Azure Virtual Desktop Specialty (AZ-140), Azure Administrator Associate</li>
    <li><strong>Citrix:</strong> Certified Professional – Virtualization (CCP-V), Certified Associate – Virtualization (CCA-V), Citrix Virtual Apps and Desktops 7 on Citrix Cloud</li>
    <li><strong>Nerdio:</strong> Nerdio Engineer</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
